### 2. Copying and Advertising Restrictions
No one has permission to advertise, replicate, monetize, or copy this project or any part thereof without prior written permission from the owner (**Aarav Ravindra Kharade**).

### 3. Contribution Guidelines and Code Attribution
All contributors must strictly adhere to the following attribution protocols:
- **New Files**: Any newly created file must include the following attribution comment at the top:
  `// <YOUR NAME> <YEAR>`
- **Modifications / Edits**: If an existing file or portion of code is modified, the contributor must mark the edited section with:
  `// <YOUR NAME> <YEAR>`
  ... edited code ...
  `// End of contribution!`
- **Commit Messages**: All git commit messages must explicitly state the contributor's full Name, the Year, the Month, and the Day (e.g., `[Aarav Ravindra Kharade - 2026-09-07] Feature update`).

### 4. Policy on Forks and Derivatives
- **Zero Support**: All forks and downstream distributions will receive **0 support** from the original author and are deemed completely **unofficial**.
- **Copyright Protection & Trademark Enforcement**: If forks copy the content, name, trademarks, branding, or features—either verbatim ("as is") or in the same manner under slight variations—they are strictly subject to copyright infringement claims and legal action.
- **Mandatory Attribution**: All forks must give prominent credit to the creator (**Aarav Ravindra Kharade**) and clearly mention the original work.
- **Unmodified CREDITS.md**: All forks MUST retain and contain the `CREDITS.md` file at the root of the main project directory exactly as is, without modification, deletion, or omission.

